  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "When counting from \\(3\\) to \\(201,\\) \\(53\\) is the \\(51\\)st number counted. When counting backwards from \\(201\\) to \\(3,\\) \\(53\\) is the \\(n\\)th number counted. What is \\(n?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(146\\)",
    "B": "\\(147\\)",
    "C": "\\(148\\)",
    "D": "\\(149\\)",
    "E": "\\(150\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Counting backward from \\(201\\), we take \\(201-53=148\\) steps to reach \\(53\\). Since \\(201\\) itself is the first number counted, the position is one greater than the number of steps. Thus\n\\[\nn=148+1=149,\n\\]\nwhich is choice D.",
